      "description": "This study sought to assess the impact of local programs that ensure\r\nthat legal counsel is provided at first appearance (usually arraignment) in\r\ncourt on court decisions (such as bail or pretrial release, and consequences\r\nsuch as pretrial detention and booking at a local detention facility), as well\r\nas on subsequent consequences for charge reduction, disposition, and\r\nsentencing.  The project collected original data from six upstate New York counties (under pseudonyms). The data were collected from indigent defense programs' case files, supplemented by data from county detention facilities on booking and\r\nrelease.\r\nDemographic variables in this collection include defendant age, race, gender, and residency.",
